{"type":"reasoning","timestamp":1788464127286,"sessionID":"ses_f973b7d37ffeZEidu0wFrEi21f","part":{"id":"prt_068c4d526001efVDMLB5gDysBd","messageID":"msg_068c4d254001l5PTePw0Xb8aan","sessionID":"ses_f973b7d37ffeZEidu0wFrEi21f","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I understand the issues. Let me analyze:\n\n1. **`**kwargs` handling in `_check_model_params`**: When a model's `__init__` has `**kwargs`, the parameter checker flags:\n   - \"Missing required model parameter: kwargs\" — because `kwargs` has no default and isn't in `model_params`. Need to exclude `kwargs` from required parameter checks (check `model_parameters[name].kind == inspect.Parameter.VAR_KEYWORD`).\n   - Also, when `kwargs` is present, extra params should be allowed (not raise \"Invalid model parameter\").\n\n2. **Remove the conditional hooks warning**: The warning about conditional hook usage. Let me search for it. This relates to `solara.use_effect` being called conditionally or a warning from solara \"Conditional hook usage\" — actually in Mesa's history, there was a fix: \"Remove warning about conditional hooks\". Let me search the codebase for \"conditional\".\n\nLet me look at git log for the warning.","time":{"start":1788464125222,"end":1788464127280},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I understand the issues. Let me analyze:\n\n1. **`**kwargs` handling in `_check_model_params`**: When a model's `__init__` has `**kwargs`, the parameter checker flags:\n   - \"Missing required model parameter: kwargs\" — because `kwargs` has no default and isn't in `model_params`. Need to exclude `kwargs` from required parameter checks (check `model_parameters[name].kind == inspect.Parameter.VAR_KEYWORD`).\n   - Also, when `kwargs` is present, extra params should be allowed (not raise \"Invalid model parameter\").\n\n2. **Remove the conditional hooks warning**: The warning about conditional hook usage. Let me search for it. This relates to `solara.use_effect` being cal