ng conditional hooks?\" warning, and correctly initializes parameter tracking whether or not initial parameters are provided.\n   - `_check_model_params`: `kwargs` is excluded from required-parameter checks, and extra parameters are allowed when the constructor signature contains `**kwargs`.\n\n2. `tests/test_solara_viz.py`: added `ModelWithKwargs` test coverage.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}}}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788464413872,"sessionID":"ses_f973b7d37ffeZEidu0wFrEi21f","part":{"id":"prt_068c92d0d001ItmSssEvxnvhU5","messageID":"msg_068c91a8c001cRJQXKb7DLAdAo","sessionID":"ses_f973b7d37ffeZEidu0wFrEi21f","type":"text","text":"Done. The fix matches upstream Mesa commit `0c1ccd68` (\"solaraviz kwargs related bugfix #2463\") exactly, and all verification passes:\n\n**Changes in `mesa/visualization/solara_viz.py`:**\n1. **Conditional hooks warning removed** (`ModelController` :194, `ModelCreator` :310) — `solara.use_reactive()` is now called unconditionally instead of only inside `if model_parameters is None:`, eliminating the hook-count mismatch that triggered reacton's \"Are you using conditional hooks?\" warning, and initializing parameter tracking correctly whether initial params are provided or not.\n2. **`**kwargs` handling in `_check_model_params`** (:350, :354):\n   - `kwargs` is excluded from required-parameter checks (no more false \"Missing required model parameter: kwargs\")\n   - When the constructor has `**kwargs`, extra parameters are allowed (no false \"Invalid model parameter\" errors)\n   - Genuine missing-required and invalid-name errors still raise\n\n**Tests** in `tests/test_solara_viz.py`: added `ModelWithKwargs` covering kwargs models with and without provided params.\n\nVerified: all 7 solara_viz tests pass, ruff check/format clean, and end-to-end rendering of a `**kwargs` model (non-reactive with params, reactive with params, and no params) produces no errors and no conditional-hook warnings.","time":{"start":1788464409869,"end":1788464413867}}}
